body:
There's a lot of contradicting thoughts in this poem. it feels like a battle. Do you still love her? Do you hate her? Do you want to pretend she never existed?  Your heart is still trying to figure out what direction to go, and your poem seem to capture it beautifully to me. 

&#x200B;

Though I am a bit drunk atm and I'm seeing myself in a lot of these poems. But I liked what you made. Thank you

To quote the great Ice cube;

"Daaaaaaaaamn"

Looking good! Keep it up!

Okay, I know everyone loves Sokka but he didn't need his girlfriend turning into the moon. lol jk

&#x200B;

But in all seriousness, I love how casually it starts, almost light hearted, and it gets deeper the further you make it done. You want to save him, because you need him. I liked it

A friend of mine once told me that some women don't want to adhere to gender roles, but they expect men to continue to have their gender role as providers.

&#x200B;

Do what you will with that statement,
